Z||000018||Shiner||02-15-2000||11:32 PM||||Monkeyman,<P> It's an alloy of magnesium.  So sue me. lol<BR>I checked out an American Racing rim at the pep boys.  I thought "pretty nice rim, is it aluminum [alloy]?)  That sucker weighed more than my 15" rim AND tire combined!  It said "alloy" on it... yeah, probably an alloy of lead!  ||||reg||12
Z||000019||Standard||02-16-2000||01:37 AM||||Alloy wheels are actually pretty heavy.  By feel, I'd have to say the 15" lace wheels on my GT outweigh the 13" steel wheels on my 84 by at least a few pounds each.  I was surprised at how heavy they were.  But they sure do look a heck of a lot better..<P>Yeah, 84 decklid grills were magnesium alloy.  Pontiac won a design award for that one.  <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 02-16-2000).]||||reg||1
